{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Sorry we're late, doctor. Err, the robot by the Engen was out and the traffic was hectic.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right. Sit down.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (NURSE): Sorry, quick one. I've just done his vitals. Blood pressure is one thirty eight over 84, pulse is seventy six.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (DOCTOR): What's the problem.",
  "[SEG0005] person_4 (PATIENT): Ag, it's nothing. She dragged me in.",
  "[SEG0006] person_1 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Ag, don't listen to him. Just tell the man.",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (DOCTOR): I'm listening.",
  "[SEG0008] person_4 (PATIENT): Ja well. It's this ringing in my right ear. Been a month. Nothing serious, hey.",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (DOCTOR): All the time?",
  "[SEG0010] person_4 (PATIENT): Umm, pretty much all the time. Worse when it's quiet, like at night. Daytime with the machines I don't even notice it.",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (DOCTOR): Machines at work.",
  "[SEG0012] person_4 (PATIENT): Ja, panel beating. The grinders and that, proper loud. I don't wear the ear things. They itch.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (FAMILY_MEMBER): I've told him. He just laughs it off.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (DOCTOR): Hearing muffled?",
  "[SEG0015] person_4 (PATIENT): A little, on the right. I can hear fine. It's not like I'm deaf or something.",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (DOCTOR): Sore?",
  "[SEG0017] person_4 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (DOCTOR): Discharge?",
  "[SEG0019] person_4 (PATIENT): No, no gunk.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (DOCTOR): Fever?",
  "[SEG0021] person_4 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (DOCTOR): Dizzy? Room spinning?",
  "[SEG0023] person_4 (PATIENT): No, the room's not spinning. Err, maybe a bit light-headed if I stand up quick. Ag, it's nothing.",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any medicines?",
  "[SEG0025] person_4 (PATIENT): No. I don't take stuff.",
  "[SEG0026] person_1 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He does. Enalopril, for his blood pressure, every morning.",
  "[SEG0027] person_4 (PATIENT): Oh. Ja. Ten milligrams. Hardly counts as a medicine.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (DOCTOR): Allergies?",
  "[SEG0029] person_4 (PATIENT): No. None.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (DOCTOR): Let me look in the ears.",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (DOCTOR): Canals clear, no wax. Drums normal both sides. No redness.",
  "[SEG0032] person_4 (PATIENT): See. I'm fine.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He said the bakkie was fine too, and it died at the robot.",
  "[SEG0034] person_4 (PATIENT): Speaking of that, did you catch the Proteas last night? That chase was lekker.",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He had the radio blasting the whole way here, shouting at the umpire.",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (DOCTOR): I saw the last few overs. Decent knock.",
  "[SEG0037] person_4 (PATIENT): And the weather at the Wanderers looked perfect. Not this wind.",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (DOCTOR): Mm. Anyway. This is most likely noise-related ringing from the workshop. I can't exclude some hearing loss till we test.",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (DOCTOR): I'm referring you for a hearing test. Audiology. They'll book it at the desk.",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (DOCTOR): We might do a scan if the hearing test is not right. Not booking that now.",
  "[SEG0041] person_2 (DOCTOR): Come back in four weeks with the results. And wear proper ear muffs at work, every shift.",
  "[SEG0042] person_4 (PATIENT): Ja ja. If I remember. Sharp, doc."
 ],
